{"runSplitQuery pre-interpolates with datasource.applyTemplateVariables, but datasource.runQuery still calls DataSourceWithBackend.query which applies the same interpolation/addAdHocFilters again before hitting the backend, causing ad hoc filters to be appended/escaped twice for every split request": 0.20364952087402344, "runShardSplitQuery calls applyTemplateVariables before computing shards, but applyTemplateVariables intentionally leaves $__range/$__auto untouched. When splitQueriesByStreamShard later runs getSelectorForShardValues it sees selectors still containing those literals, so fetchLabelValues uses an invalid stream selector and never discovers shards for queries that reference $__range/$__auto in matchers, silently breaking sharding for those queries": 0.09405270963907242}